  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Getty entered his father’s oil business and earned his first million through a successful Oklahoma lease. He continued drilling independently, acquired control of numerous companies and integrated exploration, production, transport and refining. A concession in the Neutral Zone between Saudi Arabia and Kuwait produced enormous reserves and transformed the scale of his fortune.\n\nHe also assembled a major collection of antiquities, European decorative arts and paintings. A museum opened at his Malibu property during his lifetime, while his will transferred an extraordinary endowment to the J. Paul Getty Trust. The resulting museum, research, conservation and grantmaking institutions gave his private collecting a global public reach. His legacy therefore combines aggressive petroleum investment with one of the largest philanthropic structures devoted to visual culture.",
    "html": "<p>Getty entered his father’s oil business and earned his first million through a successful Oklahoma lease. He continued drilling independently, acquired control of numerous companies and integrated exploration, production, transport and refining. A concession in the Neutral Zone between Saudi Arabia and Kuwait produced enormous reserves and transformed the scale of his fortune.</p>\r\n<p>He also assembled a major collection of antiquities, European decorative arts and paintings. A museum opened at his Malibu property during his lifetime, while his will transferred an extraordinary endowment to the J. Paul Getty Trust. The resulting museum, research, conservation and grantmaking institutions gave his private collecting a global public reach. His legacy therefore combines aggressive petroleum investment with one of the largest philanthropic structures devoted to visual culture.</p>\r\n",
